"Olget-ovekondo is Tass-ovekondo's son, a barely competent wizard with a lime green auriad."
"He wanted to inherit the village, but neither his mother nor its people would back him."
"He finds knights' bound authority revolting and called the Here-to-There a betrayal."
"He took over Alden's train room until Bithe threw him out."
"He secretly broke Uro-bor's bound wand with a striking spell sung through walls."
"Stuart and Alden accused him before executioner Vill-ma and refused to unsay it."
"Vill-ma sentenced him to labor longer than his natural life, called a gentle sentence."
